Poisoning is one of the main instakill annoyances, especially in the
mid-stages of the games.  First of all, it's a good idea to avoid
monsters with poisoned missile weapons, like the mordor orcs.  You
should try to use dorways to your advantage, by staying out of the
orc's line of fire, or run around other monsters/pets.  Secondly, you
need poison resistance.  That is the only way AFAIK to prevent
poisoning deaths.  The caveman class has this intrinsic at the
beginning of the game, but for other classes you need to eat poisoned
monsters, e.g. killer bees.  This will usually have a harmful effect,
by decreasing strength, so you should try to have a way of reversing
that effect (see spoiler later).  After a few tries, you should get a
message that the poison does not seem to affect you, and then you know
you have the 'resist poison' intrinsic.





spoiler warning






To reverse the strength loss from eating poison, and other ill effects,
get a blessed unicorn horn and apply it repeatedly.  A normal one works
to, but has less chance of working for each try.  Just be careful not
to kill a co-aligned unicorn yourself, 'cause this will anger your god
(just let your pet do it if you can).



